#6961
On the River of Thermodon.~
     Black-onyx water flows toward the southwest.  The sunlight,
reflecting off the water, forces you to squint as you travel the
river's length.  A white sand creates the river's banks.  You are
reminded of an old legend that speaks of a black river and how it
is the only way in and out of the Amazon Valley.
~
